This repository contains Lean files that are derived from OpenAI's Lean library:
github.com/openai/math, commit 3344da59991ed94f9ba711217b29c1d760badfa6, folder lean/.
That library is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of the license is in the file LICENSE.

Files of this repository that contain code copied from that library, and what was changed
(Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):

- lean/OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerScaled/ScaledParameters.lean
  Copied from lean/OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerCounterexample/ParameterExistence.lean.
  Changed: the fixed marginal cap bp 1000 is a parameter c. The names Ribbon, seed_ribbon,
  exists_parameters and floor_supply became RibbonAt, seed_ribbon_at, exists_parameters_at and the
  private floor_supply'. The definition birthG is imported, not repeated.
- lean/OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerScaled/ScaledTransfer.lean
  Copied from lean/OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerCounterexample/FiniteGraphTransfer.lean.
  Changed: the theorem transfer became transfer_div, with the threshold m/Q in place of m/100.
  The private helper lemmas are unchanged.
- lean/OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerScaled/ScaledExponential.lean
  Adapted from lean/OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerCounterexample/ExponentialGraphTransfer.lean.
  Changed: the theorem transfer_scales became transfer_scales_div, with the cap bp (12*Q+1) in place of
  bp 1000 and the threshold m/Q in place of m/100. The definitions ord, cast_ord and tendsto_ord are
  imported, not repeated.
- lean/OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerScaled/Main.lean
  The theorem exists_graphs_div is adapted from exists_graphs in
  lean/OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerCounterexample/Main.lean. The other four theorems are new.
- Challenge/Statement.lean
  The definitions IsTouchingMatching, connectedMatchingNumber, HasCliqueMinor and hadwigerNumber are
  copied unchanged from lean/ComparatorChallenges/HadwigerCounterexample.lean. The three theorem
  statements are new.

The exact changes are in lean/provenance.diff. They were made on 25 November 2026.

The 288 unchanged OpenAI files that the proof imports are not included in this repository.
lean/assemble.sh copies them from a checkout of openai/math at the commit above and checks them
against lean/OAI-SHA256SUMS.

The files listed above are not OpenAI's work. OpenAI has not reviewed or endorsed them. They use the
Lean namespace OAI and the folder OAI/Combinatorics/ only so that they compile next to OpenAI's
library and can use its names.
